      "items": [
        {
          "id": "019bdbb9-669c-77c1-aa4f-3b70df02f5f3",
          "hidden": false,
          "company": "TransUnion",
          "position": "Senior Software Engineer",
          "location": "",
          "period": "Jan 2021 – Present",
          "website": {
            "url": "",
            "label": "",
            "inlineLink": false
          },
          "description": "<p>Led backend modernisation and developer productivity initiatives across multiple business domains, primarily using .NET and Azure.</p><p>Primary skills used: C# 14, .NET 8/10, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://ASP.NET\">ASP.NET</a> Core, Azure Service Fabric, KeyVault, Application Insights, API Management, .NET Aspire, Service Bus, C++, OpenApi, Octopus Deploy, MySql, TDD, DDD and BDD</p><ul><li><p>Increased release cadence from quarterly to weekly by decomposing a C++/VB.NET/C# monolith into domain-aligned .NET microservices within a Service Fabric cluster.</p></li><li><p>Championed PR-gated CI/CD and trunk-based development practices, reducing downstream breaking-change issues and improving release confidence.</p></li><li><p>Balanced the added operational complexity of microservices through automated integration testing, API versioning, and feature flags.</p></li><li><p>Reduced CI/CD pipeline runtime by ~50% through build/test optimisation and pipeline redesign, shortening feedback loops and merge-to-production time.</p></li><li><p>Modernised A/B comparison tooling by replacing a legacy tool with a new one, built as a series of CLI tools with a bundled Blazor report for easy comparisons by QA, containing features such as accepted difference handling, ignore rules, and PII data masking. Cutting comparison runtime by ~30 minutes and reducing validation effort by several hours per release.</p></li><li><p>Engineered an automated AI workflow that utilizes the Azure DevOps REST API to extract tech debt items, transform them into structured LLM prompts, and execute autonomous resolution via a custom background CLI tool.</p></li><li><p>Mentored engineers regularly, onboarded two cross-functional teams, including our global teams. Acted as tech lead for a month, contributed to hiring interviews, and regularly aligned technical implementation with product and operational stakeholders.</p></li><li><p>Resolved a challenge with our local development and testing practises by engineering a .NET Aspire solution for our distributed system to help improve local development across our connected services.</p></li><li><p>Supported out-of-hours live releases, such as SQL Server migrations and new product releases.</p></li></ul><p></p>",
          "roles": []
        },
        {
          "id": "019bdbbc-f009-7056-ad8d-4d34311e0ea0",
          "hidden": false,
          "company": "CallCredit",
          "position": "Software Engineer",
          "location": "",
          "period": "Jan 2016 – Jan 2021",
          "website": {
            "url": "",
            "label": "",
            "inlineLink": false
          },
          "description": "<p>Delivered platform and tooling improvements enabling the cloud migration and microservices re-architecture.</p><p>Primary skills used: C#, <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://ASP.NET\">ASP.NET</a> (many versions), C++, COM+, VB6, Azure KeyVault, Application Insights, MySql</p><ul><li><p>Provided care and maintenance to a SOAP, COM+ live system.</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Led TFVC -&gt; Git migration and introduced trunk-based development to support faster merges and continuous delivery.</p></li><li><p>Introduced EF Core patterns and telemetry on slow queries to prioritise fixes and improve troubleshooting speed.</p></li><li><p>Implemented SpecFlow-based BDD tests across various domains.</p></li><li><p>Contributed to the rollout of OAuth/OpenID Connect for securing our APIs.</p></li><li><p>Led an interactive Game Jam, building a tower defence game using MonoGame.NET, that could be played by programming against an API running alongside the game.</p></li><li><p>Took part as a buddy in the graduate programme, offering support and guidance to new graduates.</p></li></ul><p></p>",
          "roles": []
